  "title": "NEWLEADER ACK is sent before the DIFF-synchronized history is durable",
  "cause": "Learner.syncWithLeader hands buffered proposals to FollowerZooKeeperServer.logRequest, which only enqueues to SyncRequestProcessor, and writes the NEWLEADER ACK without waiting for append/fsync; currentEpoch is already persisted.",
  "trigger": "A leader with an uncommitted logged txn is re-elected; a follower DIFF-syncs it, ACKs NEWLEADER (counted toward the quorum, leader serves the txn) and crashes before SyncThread forces the log; it restarts with the new epoch and, with another server lacking the txn, elects a new leader.",
  "consequence": "A transaction the previous leader already served after its NEWLEADER quorum is missing at the next leader (lost or truncated cluster-wide).",
  "sites": [
    "Learner.java:syncWithLeader NEWLEADER case",
    "FollowerZooKeeperServer.java:logRequest",
    "SyncRequestProcessor.java:flush",
    "Leader.java:waitForNewLeaderAck"
  ],
  "actions": [
    "LearnerNewLeader",
    "LearnerAckNewLeader",
    "LeaderBroadcast",
    "FsyncOne",
    "Crash"
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "NewLeaderAckDurable",
    "CommittedSurvivesLeaderChange"
  ],
  "premises": [
    "The NEWLEADER ACK is written without waiting for the SyncRequestProcessor flush of the handed-off proposals.",
    "The leader counts that ACK toward its NEWLEADER quorum and then serves its initial history.",
    "Fail-stop crashes lose appended-but-unforced log records; currentEpoch is persisted before the ACK."
  ],
